1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,740
In GTA 6, stealing a car doesn't make

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,481
it yours. Leave it behind, die, or quit

3
00:00:05,481 --> 00:00:08,221
the game, and that car is gone. So

4
00:00:08,221 --> 00:00:10,961
in this video: how to steal smart, how

5
00:00:10,961 --> 00:00:13,702
to keep a car forever, and which cars

6
00:00:13,702 --> 00:00:15,072
are actually worth keeping.

7
00:00:15,322 --> 00:00:18,197
We'll cover the Waink scanner, every way into

8
00:00:18,197 --> 00:00:21,072
a car, trackers, registering with Moses, garages, and

9
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:23,947
then the best cars by the game's own

10
00:00:23,947 --> 00:00:26,822
ratings. Stick around, because one tracker type can

11
00:00:26,822 --> 00:00:28,978
bring the police straight to you.

12
00:00:29,228 --> 00:00:31,921
Step one is the Waink app on your

13
00:00:31,921 --> 00:00:34,615
phone. Open your phone with up on the

14
00:00:34,615 --> 00:00:37,308
d-pad, then scan a car. It shows the

15
00:00:37,308 --> 00:00:40,002
car's stats, its condition, and its security, including

16
00:00:40,002 --> 00:00:41,012
alarms and trackers.

17
00:00:41,262 --> 00:00:43,484
It also tells you what the car sells

18
00:00:43,484 --> 00:00:45,705
for and what it costs to register. That

19
00:00:45,705 --> 00:00:47,927
one scan tells you whether a car is

20
00:00:47,927 --> 00:00:50,149
a quick payday, a keeper, or a waste

21
00:00:50,149 --> 00:00:50,982
of your time.

22
00:00:51,232 --> 00:00:53,444
And if you're already driving, press down to

23
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:55,656
check for a tracker. Get in the habit

24
00:00:55,656 --> 00:00:57,868
of checking before you get attached to a

25
00:00:57,868 --> 00:00:58,144
car.

26
00:00:58,394 --> 00:01:00,842
Two more Waink tricks most players miss. Stand

27
00:01:00,842 --> 00:01:03,290
near a car you've already been in and

28
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:05,738
press L1 to see its engine details. And

29
00:01:05,738 --> 00:01:08,186
while driving, hold left on the d-pad to

30
00:01:08,186 --> 00:01:10,634
bring the car's info up on your screen.

31
00:01:10,884 --> 00:01:13,801
Now, getting in. First, just try the door.

32
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:16,717
Some parked cars are unlocked, and that's the

33
00:01:16,717 --> 00:01:18,540
quietest theft in the game.

34
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:21,536
If it's locked, you can smash the window.

35
00:01:21,536 --> 00:01:24,283
It's fast, but it can trigger the alarm,

36
00:01:24,283 --> 00:01:26,686
and an alarm alerts the people nearby.

37
00:01:26,936 --> 00:01:30,075
Locked cars also need hotwiring. Push both sticks

38
00:01:30,075 --> 00:01:33,214
together to fill the semi-circles and the engine

39
00:01:33,214 --> 00:01:35,960
starts. Most older cars can be hotwired.

40
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:39,052
High-end keyless cars are different. You can't hotwire

41
00:01:39,052 --> 00:01:41,893
them. You need a key cloner, which unlocks

42
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:44,735
later in the story through Randy, the contact

43
00:01:44,735 --> 00:01:46,866
who hands out high-end car contracts.

44
00:01:47,116 --> 00:01:49,583
And of course, you can still carjack. Pull

45
00:01:49,583 --> 00:01:52,050
the driver out and the car is yours,

46
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:53,284
at least for now.

47
00:01:53,534 --> 00:01:56,163
Here's the trap I mentioned. There are two

48
00:01:56,163 --> 00:01:58,792
kinds of tracker. A standard tracker just stops

49
00:01:58,792 --> 00:02:01,421
you from modifying the car until it's registered

50
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:02,078
to you.

51
00:02:02,328 --> 00:02:04,999
An advanced tracker is the dangerous one. It's

52
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:07,669
common on high-end cars, it notifies the police

53
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:10,340
when the car is stolen, and it reports

54
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,010
the car's location unless you're moving at high

55
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:13,344
speed.

56
00:02:13,594 --> 00:02:15,941
Red Bull's guide adds that an advanced tracker

57
00:02:15,941 --> 00:02:18,287
pings the police once the car gets too

58
00:02:18,287 --> 00:02:20,634
far from where you took it. So the

59
00:02:20,634 --> 00:02:22,981
longer and slower your drive home, the worse

60
00:02:22,981 --> 00:02:25,327
it gets. Either drive fast, or don't take

61
00:02:25,327 --> 00:02:26,794
it in the first place.

62
00:02:27,044 --> 00:02:29,742
So if you steal a tracked supercar, keep

63
00:02:29,742 --> 00:02:32,439
your foot down. Slow down in traffic and

64
00:02:32,439 --> 00:02:33,788
you're broadcasting your position.

65
00:02:34,038 --> 00:02:37,238
In Chapter 1 you can still drive other

66
00:02:37,238 --> 00:02:40,438
cars around Leonida, just only temporarily. So enjoy

67
00:02:40,438 --> 00:02:43,638
them, but don't get attached until registration unlocks.

68
00:02:43,888 --> 00:02:47,240
Now the part most people miss: keeping a

69
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,592
car. Registration unlocks in Chapter 2, at Moses's

70
00:02:50,592 --> 00:02:53,945
garage in Port Gellhorn, after his introductory mission.

71
00:02:53,945 --> 00:02:57,297
Before that, in Chapter 1, Jason's starting car

72
00:02:57,297 --> 00:02:59,392
is your main personal vehicle.

73
00:02:59,642 --> 00:03:02,698
The process is simple. Drive a car without

74
00:03:02,698 --> 00:03:05,755
a tracker into Moses's workshop, choose Respray, pick

75
00:03:05,755 --> 00:03:08,811
a new colour, then choose Register. Your first

76
00:03:08,811 --> 00:03:11,868
registration during that mission is free, so pick

77
00:03:11,868 --> 00:03:13,778
a car you actually love.

78
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:16,925
After that, registering costs money. The Waink scan

79
00:03:16,925 --> 00:03:19,823
shows you the price before you steal, and

80
00:03:19,823 --> 00:03:21,996
cheaper cars cost less to register.

81
00:03:22,246 --> 00:03:24,942
Pay N Spray can register cars too, and

82
00:03:24,942 --> 00:03:27,639
it can sell them for cash. But depending

83
00:03:27,639 --> 00:03:29,998
on the tracker, some vehicles get refused.

84
00:03:30,248 --> 00:03:33,017
Why does registering matter so much? Registered cars

85
00:03:33,017 --> 00:03:35,787
can be modified, and if you lose one,

86
00:03:35,787 --> 00:03:38,556
you can always get it back. An unregistered

87
00:03:38,556 --> 00:03:41,326
stolen car that gets destroyed is gone for

88
00:03:41,326 --> 00:03:41,672
good.

89
00:03:41,922 --> 00:03:44,236
Found something special but can't afford to register

90
00:03:44,236 --> 00:03:46,550
it yet? The safest move is to park

91
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:48,864
it in your garage and leave it there

92
00:03:48,864 --> 00:03:51,178
until you have the cash. Driving it around

93
00:03:51,178 --> 00:03:52,914
before that puts it at risk.

94
00:03:53,164 --> 00:03:55,655
Once a car is registered, the Scooter Bros

95
00:03:55,655 --> 00:03:58,146
app lets you summon it any time. And

96
00:03:58,146 --> 00:04:00,636
your personal vehicle carries spare outfits in its

97
00:04:00,636 --> 00:04:03,127
trunk, which is a lifesaver when the police

98
00:04:03,127 --> 00:04:04,684
are looking for your clothes.

99
00:04:04,934 --> 00:04:07,920
You also need space. Every registered car needs

100
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,906
a free garage spot. Garages store your cars

101
00:04:10,906 --> 00:04:13,892
for free, hold your weapon loadout, and let

102
00:04:13,892 --> 00:04:15,758
you drop off illegal goods.

103
00:04:16,008 --> 00:04:18,708
More space comes as the story moves on,

104
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:21,407
including Valentina's garage later in the game. So

105
00:04:21,407 --> 00:04:24,107
if your slots are full, keep playing the

106
00:04:24,107 --> 00:04:26,807
main missions before you start selling off your

107
00:04:26,807 --> 00:04:27,144
favourites.

108
00:04:27,394 --> 00:04:30,312
You can only buy garages after Jason and

109
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:33,231
Lucia leave Key Lento, and buying every garage

110
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:36,149
unlocks an achievement called Little Boxes. So start

111
00:04:36,149 --> 00:04:38,338
saving early if you're a collector.

112
00:04:38,588 --> 00:04:41,296
And for repairs and customisation there are Pay

113
00:04:41,296 --> 00:04:44,004
N Spray locations all over the map, nineteen

114
00:04:44,004 --> 00:04:46,712
of them according to MetaForge's count, so you're

115
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:48,404
never far from a fix.

116
00:04:48,654 --> 00:04:51,672
Now, which cars are worth a garage spot?

117
00:04:51,672 --> 00:04:54,690
A quick warning first: Rockstar hasn't published top

118
00:04:54,690 --> 00:04:57,708
speeds, so instead I'll use the speed ratings

119
00:04:57,708 --> 00:05:00,726
the game itself shows, as recorded by GamerBlurb.

120
00:05:00,976 --> 00:05:04,085
The highest speed rating so far belongs to

121
00:05:04,085 --> 00:05:07,194
the Pegassi Infernus 96, at 7.1 out of

122
00:05:07,194 --> 00:05:10,303
10. It's the Lamborghini Diablo-style exotic, and right

123
00:05:10,303 --> 00:05:13,024
now it's the pick for raw speed.

124
00:05:13,274 --> 00:05:16,580
Next is the Grotti Cheetah 95 at 6.6,

125
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:19,886
but that one is an Ultimate Edition car,

126
00:05:19,886 --> 00:05:23,192
so not everyone has it. Then the Pfister

127
00:05:23,192 --> 00:05:26,499
Comet 88 at 6.1, the classic Porsche 911-style

128
00:05:26,499 --> 00:05:29,805
sports car, and a great all-rounder for everyday

129
00:05:29,805 --> 00:05:30,218
driving.

130
00:05:30,468 --> 00:05:33,797
For classic style, the Invetero Coquette 64 rates

131
00:05:33,797 --> 00:05:37,127
5.9, the Corvette C2 look. The Annis Elegy

132
00:05:37,127 --> 00:05:40,456
90 and the Bravado Buffalo 19 both sit

133
00:05:40,456 --> 00:05:43,786
at 5.5, so you get a Nissan Skyline-style

134
00:05:43,786 --> 00:05:47,115
car or a Dodge Charger-style four-door muscle car

135
00:05:47,115 --> 00:05:48,780
with the same speed.

136
00:05:49,030 --> 00:05:53,110
Muscle fans get the Bravado Gauntlet Custom 69

137
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:57,190
at 5.4, the Dodge Challenger lookalike. For everyday

138
00:05:57,190 --> 00:06:01,270
driving, the Pfister Astron, a Porsche Macan-style SUV,

139
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:05,350
and the Obey 8F Drafter, an Audi RS5-style

140
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:07,390
coupe, both rate 5.3.

141
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,407
And if you go off-road, especially in the

142
00:06:10,407 --> 00:06:13,174
Grassrivers or up near Mount Kalaga, the BF

143
00:06:13,174 --> 00:06:15,941
Bandito 77 is slow on the road, but

144
00:06:15,941 --> 00:06:18,708
its off-road score is far higher than its

145
00:06:18,708 --> 00:06:19,400
road score.

146
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:22,692
Don't forget Jason's own car, the Vapid Ganado

147
00:06:22,692 --> 00:06:25,735
70. It's no speed machine at 4.7, but

148
00:06:25,735 --> 00:06:28,777
it's his personal vehicle from the start and

149
00:06:28,777 --> 00:06:29,538
it's free.

150
00:06:29,788 --> 00:06:32,443
One more thing: cars in GTA 6 need

151
00:06:32,443 --> 00:06:35,098
fuel, and electric ones need charging. A supercar

152
00:06:35,098 --> 00:06:37,753
with an empty tank is just an expensive

153
00:06:37,753 --> 00:06:40,408
statue, so keep an eye on it before

154
00:06:40,408 --> 00:06:41,404
a big job.

155
00:06:41,654 --> 00:06:44,557
Not every car should be kept. Moses also

156
00:06:44,557 --> 00:06:47,461
buys stolen cars, but only ones without a

157
00:06:47,461 --> 00:06:50,364
tracker, and after a sale he goes on

158
00:06:50,364 --> 00:06:53,267
cooldown. Sleep at a safehouse and the cooldown

159
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:53,630
resets.

160
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:56,555
Pay N Spray buys cars too, but it

161
00:06:56,555 --> 00:06:59,230
has a daily limit and won't take high-end

162
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:01,904
cars with trackers. And later, Randy's high-end contracts

163
00:07:01,904 --> 00:07:03,576
pay the most of all.

164
00:07:03,826 --> 00:07:07,026
So the rule is simple: tracker-free and fun

165
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:10,226
to drive, keep it. Tracked, or just average,

166
00:07:10,226 --> 00:07:11,026
sell it.

167
00:07:11,276 --> 00:07:14,094
Your car choice matters for crimes too. Older

168
00:07:14,094 --> 00:07:16,913
cars you can hotwire are safer for jobs

169
00:07:16,913 --> 00:07:19,731
than luxury cars, which need a cloned key

170
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:21,140
and often carry trackers.

171
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:24,233
For robberies, think about space. Each character carries

172
00:07:24,233 --> 00:07:27,075
two stash bags, a van or truck holds

173
00:07:27,075 --> 00:07:29,918
up to eight, and a motorbike holds none.

174
00:07:29,918 --> 00:07:32,761
Bring a bike to a jewellery job and

175
00:07:32,761 --> 00:07:34,182
you're leaving money behind.

176
00:07:34,432 --> 00:07:37,412
But for escaping at three stars or more,

177
00:07:37,412 --> 00:07:40,392
a normal car struggles. A fast bike, or

178
00:07:40,392 --> 00:07:43,000
going on foot through alleys, works better.

179
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:46,288
So here's my advice. Don't burn your free

180
00:07:46,288 --> 00:07:49,325
registration on the first shiny car you see.

181
00:07:49,325 --> 00:07:52,363
Scan a few, check for trackers, and register

182
00:07:52,363 --> 00:07:53,882
something fast and tracker-free.

183
00:07:54,132 --> 00:07:57,108
Sell the tracked cars instead of keeping them,

184
00:07:57,108 --> 00:08:00,084
use older hotwireable cars for crimes, and keep

185
00:08:00,084 --> 00:08:03,060
your favourite registered car clean for driving around.

186
00:08:03,310 --> 00:08:05,942
And three mistakes to avoid. Mistake one: using

187
00:08:05,942 --> 00:08:08,575
your favourite registered car for a robbery. If

188
00:08:08,575 --> 00:08:11,207
the police spot it, the car becomes part

189
00:08:11,207 --> 00:08:13,840
of your heat, and the only fix is

190
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,814
to ditch it or switch cars.

191
00:08:16,064 --> 00:08:19,077
Mistake two: smashing windows in busy streets. The

192
00:08:19,077 --> 00:08:22,090
alarm alerts everyone nearby, and witnesses are how

193
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:25,103
the police find out about you in the

194
00:08:25,103 --> 00:08:25,856
first place.

195
00:08:26,106 --> 00:08:28,701
Mistake three: falling in love with a supercar

196
00:08:28,701 --> 00:08:31,296
before you scan it. If it has an

197
00:08:31,296 --> 00:08:33,891
advanced tracker, you can't simply keep it, and

198
00:08:33,891 --> 00:08:36,162
you've just painted a target on yourself.

199
00:08:36,412 --> 00:08:39,325
Quick recap. Scan with Waink. Try the door

200
00:08:39,325 --> 00:08:42,238
before smashing the window. Watch out for advanced

201
00:08:42,238 --> 00:08:45,150
trackers. Register in Chapter 2 at Moses's garage,

202
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:48,063
your first one is free. And you need

203
00:08:48,063 --> 00:08:50,976
a free garage spot for every car you

204
00:08:50,976 --> 00:08:51,340
keep.

205
00:08:51,590 --> 00:08:54,227
What's the first car you registered in GTA

206
00:08:54,227 --> 00:08:56,864
6? Tell me in the comments. And subscribe,

207
00:08:56,864 --> 00:08:59,500
because next up is every beginner tip I

208
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,478
wish I'd known on day one.
